# Subject-centered datasets

Canonical researcher-facing tree under `NEUROFLOW_DATASETS_ROOT`:

```text
<data/datasets>/<workspace>/
  sub-<id>/
    anat/ | dwi/
    derivatives/
      <package>/<module>/…     # FSL, SCT, ANTs, ITK, Slicer, …
      freesurfer/…             # recon-all native tree (mri, surf, …)
```

## Rules

- Resolve all dataset paths via `DatasetStore` — do not hardcode `derivatives/` under the workspace root.
- `derivative_dir(workspace, subject_id, package_id, module_id)` → `sub-<id>/derivatives/<package>/<module>/`.
- Every `launch_*_job` must accept `workspace` + `subject_id`, call `stage_input`, then `link_job_output_to_derivatives` (or FreeSurfer SUBJECTS_DIR equivalent).
- Job runtime stays under `data/jobs/<tool>/<job_id>/`; that does **not** replace the dataset tree.
- FreeSurfer: `SUBJECTS_DIR = <workspace>/sub-<id>/derivatives`, recon-all `-s freesurfer` (`FREESURFER_PIPELINE_SUBJECT`).
- New tool packages must take the same Form fields (`workspace`, `subject_id`) and follow this layout; update tests when paths change.

Legacy `<workspace>/derivatives/…` (sibling to subjects) is obsolete for new jobs.
